From 5905c6fbe9868dfe2dd32c18b2297ab75663caf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:11:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Emscripten: compute guest pointers with integer
 arithmetic

memory_base + guestAddress wraps around 2^32 with the rotated mapping. Pointer
overflow is undefined in C++ and LLVM optimised on it (out-of-bounds access in
coreinit's foreground bucket init), so on Emscripten memory_base is a small
class whose operator+ adds integers. Other platforms keep uint8*.
---
 .../GraphicPack/GraphicPack2PatchesApply.cpp  |  4 +--
 src/Cafe/HW/MMU/MMU.cpp                       |  6 ++--
 src/Cafe/HW/MMU/MMU.h                         |  3 +-
 src/Common/GuestMemoryBase.h                  | 33 +++++++++++++++++++
 src/Common/MemPtr.h                           |  3 +-
 5 files changed, 42 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/Common/GuestMemoryBase.h

